The audit report is written and pushed to `C:\CE_PLAN\areas\TEAM_AUDIT_T2_24OCT.md`. It covers the water-sensitive design and council rules in the installed Civil 3.0.72, plus Structural 1.0.122, which has none of this code.

It was done by reading the code only, with hand calculations. Nothing was built, tested or opened in AutoCAD, and I did not re-read the council PDFs themselves.

**Result:** 26 new findings (5 high, 10 medium, 11 low).

**Top 3:**
1. **Council minimum after-development runoff figure is never used.** Darebin's 0.8, Maribyrnong's 0.75 and Boroondara's 0.65 are stored, but CDDESIGN ignores them. A 600 m² Darebin lot is worked at 0.70 instead of 0.80, so the tank comes out too small.
2. **The rainwater-tank reuse credit never runs.** CDDESIGN never passes a tank into the credit sum, so no job ever shows a credit. The Kingston sum it would use also gives a 6,000 L tank 1.5 m³ instead of the council's 1.0 m³.
3. **The 300 mm minimum head on a charged downpipe system is never checked.** A 250 mm head passes with no warning, although the rules list prints the 300 mm as if it were enforced.

**Settings page:** still none of the runoff numbers has a box (already BUG-546), and no council value can be edited anywhere.

**Matches hand calculations:** rainfall intensity, the flow sum, orifice sizing, Boyd's storage and the Blue Factor garden/lawn fix.

**Needs Tim's word before fixing:** finding 5, the Maroondah method. Using the council's own runoff figure and storm length gives a permitted discharge of 3.68 L/s instead of CE's 5.18 L/s on a bare 600 m² lot. The same storm length also sizes the outlet pipe, so the change is Tim's call.
